{title:'Your foundations are now connected',kicker:'Next class · OpenAI coding in Python',html:()=>'<div class="grid two"><div class="panel dark stack"><h3>Explain the whole system</h3><p>Represent relevant facts. Apply justified rules. Choose actions. Measure outcomes. Check the evidence behind an answer.</p><p class="muted">Next: use these foundations when working with model prompts and Python API calls.</p></div><div class="worksheet">'+field('exitWhy','Why does an AI assistant need both a useful representation and a way to evaluate its answers?','Give one example from today’s labs.')+'<div class="row"><button id="downloadFinal" class="primary">Download my work</button><button id="sourcesBtn">Sources and coverage</button></div><div class="portfolio"><a href="knowledge_rules.py" download>Python rules</a><a href="performance_metrics.py" download>Python metrics</a></div></div></div>'+note('Carry one habit forward: explain why each fact, rule, line of code, and metric is needed.')}
